# CRLF line endings end-to-end -- ouroboros round 46 (fresh seam: byte-level
# lexing through the dual parsers; no earlier round probed it).
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is frontend-vs-canonical-lexer drift: parser.c
# skips CR exactly when the next byte is LF (lexer.c #880), and frontend.eigs
# rejected every CR -- so any Windows-edited source ran on the VM and refused
# to build. A LONE CR stays an error on BOTH sides; the mirror is the pair
# rule, not "CR is whitespace". This file itself is CRLF-ended, which is the
# whole test.
x is 2
print of x
if x > 1:
    print of "crlf-body"

define f(k) as:
    return k + 1

print of (f of x)
